Lakṣmaṇa resumes tale at Rāma bidding --- Viṣṇu cites friendship with noble Vr̥tra yet must aid gods --- Viṣṇu divides himself among Indra, thunderbolt and earth --- Gods approach Vr̥tra blazing in forest --- Terrified gods watch Indra hurl blazing vajra at Vr̥tra head --- Indra flees to world end pursued by brahmahatyā --- Indra-less gods praise Viṣṇu and beg Indra deliverance --- Viṣṇu promises horse sacrifice will restore fearless Indra